export const PITCH_SLIDE_GENERATED_ASSETS: Record<number, { imageUrl: string; narrationScript: string; narrationAudioUrl: string }> = {
  0: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-0-1773265350650.png", narrationScript: "Good morning, Kipp. It is great to sit down with you today. Thank you for carving out the time, I know exactly how valuable your schedule is right now. \n\nI want to set the tone right out of the gate. Today is not a standard media buy pitch, and I am not here to just walk you through another ad platform. This is a strategic partnership discussion about accelerating HubSpot's next major phase of growth. \n\nWe all know HubSpot is the absolute gold standard for organic marketing. Your inbound engine has successfully scaled this company past two billion in revenue and over two hundred thousand customers globally. But as you look to satisfy those aggressive new targets from the board, we are going to focus specifically on your enterprise upmarket motion. Reaching those complex, upmarket buying committees at scale requires a different lever. \n\nThat is exactly where LinkedIn comes in. Today's conversation is about how a highly targeted, data-backed LinkedIn strategy can directly complement, rather than compete with, your inbound-first philosophy. We know you are highly analytical. You need to reach elusive enterprise decision-makers in a premium, brand-safe environment, and you absolutely must see hard attribution to the pipeline. \n\nOver the next few minutes, I am going to show you exactly how we can build an enterprise growth pilot together that bridges the gap between your massive organic foundation and your upmarket revenue targets.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-0-1773281281614.wav" },
  1: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-1-1773265375914.png", narrationScript: "Let's dive right into how we've structured our time today. I've built this conversation specifically around what I understand matters most to your team right now. We'll start entirely with HubSpot's growth landscape, not ours, because I want to make sure I have the picture right. We need to align on your board's mandate to accelerate enterprise growth, while still honoring the organic, inbound engine that brought you to two billion in revenue and over two hundred thousand global customers. \n\nFrom there, we'll unpack the specific enterprise challenge. Reaching complex buying committees requires a different muscle, and we'll look at the gaps organic simply can't fill. Then, I'll share exactly where I think LinkedIn can add value. Kipp, I know you are highly metrics-driven and rightfully skeptical of paid channels that can't prove pipeline contribution. So, we'll focus heavily on audience quality, brand safety, and how our targeting complements your inbound-first philosophy without wasting a single dollar of spend. \n\nWe'll end with a concrete pilot plan. I'll show you exactly how we propose testing this motion, the specific success metrics we'll use, and how we will attribute our campaigns directly back to your enterprise pipeline. Finally, we'll map out clear next steps to get this moving.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-1-1773281330470.wav" },
  2: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-2-1773265402133.png", narrationScript: "Let's ground this conversation in where HubSpot is today, Kipp. You're sitting at $2.17 billion in ARR, growing at an impressive 20-plus percent year over year. That is a phenomenal trajectory, but we also know that kind of success brings immense pressure from the board to not just maintain, but aggressively accelerate that momentum. \n\nYou’ve built a massive global footprint with over 200,000 customers across 120 countries. And your inbound methodology is, frankly, legendary. With over 7 million monthly blog visitors, you absolutely dominate the SMB and mid-market spaces organically. You literally wrote the playbook on it. \n\nBut looking at your next phase of growth, the strategic shift is clear. You are making a very deliberate push upmarket into the enterprise space. We see this signaled strongly through your recent rollouts of Operations Hub and Commerce Hub, as well as the strategic acquisition of Clearbit. Enterprise is a different beast. Reaching those highly complex, multi-stakeholder buying committees requires a highly targeted approach, because the organic engine that won the mid-market won't always capture those specific enterprise ICPs at the scale or speed you need right now. \n\nBefore we look at how LinkedIn’s platform can specifically fuel that enterprise pipeline and complement your inbound philosophy, I want to make sure we have the foundation right. Is this picture of your current strategic focus accurate, Kipp, or is there anything you would add or correct?", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-2-1773281372398.wav" },
  3: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-3-1773265430313.png", narrationScript: "Looking at your current growth engine, Kipp, HubSpot literally wrote the book on inbound marketing. Let me be clear right out of the gate: I am absolutely not here to challenge that. \n\nYour content engine is undeniably one of the strongest in all of B2B tech. You're driving over seven million monthly blog visitors. You have millions of professionals holding HubSpot Academy certifications. That massive organic reach has built a two billion dollar revenue machine and a deeply loyal global community. \n\nSo, the question we are answering today is not whether inbound works. We already know it does. The question is whether inbound alone can reliably reach the highly-guarded enterprise buyers you are targeting next. \n\nWhen you're moving aggressively upmarket, those Fortune 500 CIOs, RevOps leaders, and VP-level decision-makers aren't always searching for solutions on Google, and they aren't always falling into traditional organic funnels. They are, however, actively engaging in peer discussions and consuming thought leadership in a brand-safe environment on LinkedIn. \n\nWhat we're talking about today isn't about replacing your inbound engine. It is about taking that incredible content you are already producing and amplifying it. We want to precision-target the exact enterprise buying committees that are historically the hardest to capture organically, and turn that engagement into measurable, attributable pipeline.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-3-1773281416004.wav" },
  4: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-4-1773265458201.png", narrationScript: "Looking at the strategic gap we uncover when moving upmarket, the dynamic completely changes. Kipp, HubSpot has undeniably mastered inbound. You've built a two-billion-dollar engine on capturing intent. But as your board pushes for aggressive enterprise growth, the playbook has to shift. \n\nWhen we look at your true enterprise buyers—the VPs and C-suite executives at companies with over a thousand employees—they simply consume content differently. They aren't going to Google and searching for \"best enterprise CRM\", and they aren't finding their next multi-million dollar tech stack through a top-of-funnel blog post. \n\nAt that level, decision-making is heavily insulated. These executives rely on closed peer networks, analyst reports, and board-level recommendations. Your organic engine captures existing demand brilliantly. If an enterprise buyer is actively looking, HubSpot will undoubtedly catch them. But for enterprise, you can't just wait for them to search. You have to proactively create that demand. You have to get your brand in front of that VP in a trusted environment before they even realize they need to replace their legacy system. \n\nSo, thinking about your current upmarket motion, how are you currently reaching those VP and C-level decision-makers at target enterprise accounts before they actively enter a buying cycle?", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-4-1773281460957.wav" },
  5: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-5-1773265483534.png", narrationScript: "Looking at your upmarket goals, Kipp, we have to talk about where your future enterprise buyers actually spend their time. Globally, LinkedIn is home to over 67 million senior-level decision-makers. But what matters isn't just the scale, it's the context. When these leaders log in daily, they aren't looking at vacation photos. They are actively consuming business content, researching trends, and solving complex operational problems. They are already in a business mindset. \n\nWe ran the numbers specifically for HubSpot's enterprise push. Right now, there are approximately 2.4 million VP-level and above professionals in IT, Marketing, Sales, and RevOps at companies with more than a thousand employees active on our platform. These are the exact buying committee members who hold the keys to those massive enterprise deals. \n\nAnd here is the reality of moving upmarket. These executives rarely fill out inbound forms. They aren't actively Googling for new CRM solutions because they already have entrenched legacy systems in place. You simply cannot reach this specific, high-value cohort at scale through organic content or Google Ads alone. \n\nTo hit the board's growth targets, you need a proactive way to get HubSpot's narrative in front of these 2.4 million leaders before they even realize they need to upgrade. LinkedIn gives you the precision to do exactly that, complementing your inbound engine by creating the enterprise demand that organic just can't catch.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-5-1773281501630.wav" },
  6: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-6-1773265512414.png", narrationScript: "Building on your incredible inbound foundation, Kipp, the hurdle with scaling HubSpot's enterprise motion is that capturing search intent alone is no longer enough. Google is fantastic at telling you someone just searched for enterprise CRM software. But who actually made that search? Was it an intern doing market research, or was it the actual decision-maker? \n\nThat is where LinkedIn fundamentally changes your paid strategy and protects your ROI. We allow you to target by professional identity. You are reaching buyers based on who they are, not just what they searched. Instead of guessing based on anonymous keywords, LinkedIn tells you with absolute certainty that your message is sitting exactly in front of the VP of Sales at a 5,000-person company who is actively making the buying decision. \n\nThis is entirely powered by deterministic, first-party data. We match your upmarket ICP against real-time data updated by the professionals themselves, including exact job titles, function, seniority, company size, industry, and specific technical skills. \n\nWhen you are closing massive enterprise deals, you don't just need a high volume of leads, you need to penetrate a complex buying committee. You need to specifically reach the CTO, the VP of RevOps, and the Head of Sales Enablement. By pivoting from broad behavioral intent to precise professional identity, we eliminate the audience waste you typically see on other paid channels, ensuring every dollar spent directly builds qualified enterprise pipeline.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-6-1773281559275.wav" },
  7: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-7-1773265534879.png", narrationScript: "Building on that inbound foundation, Kipp, I want to address the elephant in the room. HubSpot is the undisputed king of organic. You and your team already create world-class content. The State of Marketing report, the HubSpot Academy courses, the blog—it is the absolute gold standard in our industry. \n\nBut as the board pushes for aggressive upmarket growth, the gap to hitting those enterprise numbers isn't content quality. It is distribution. The Chief Revenue Officers and enterprise CMOs at billion-dollar companies aren't always actively Googling for CRM solutions or stumbling across your blog organically. \n\nThat is exactly where LinkedIn steps in. We aren't here to compete with your organic engine. We are here to amplify it. LinkedIn becomes the precision distribution channel for the massive content investments you have already made. \n\nThink of this strategy as 'paid inbound.' Instead of waiting for a high-value enterprise decision-maker to organically find your latest report, we proactively place that specific asset directly into their daily feed. We target them by their exact job title, company size, and industry. You are taking your absolute best inbound assets and putting them right in the laps of the exact buyers you need to hit your upmarket growth targets, all while tracking every single interaction directly back to closed-won pipeline.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-7-1773281606855.wav" },
  8: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-8-1773265562870.png", narrationScript: "Building on what we just discussed about enterprise reach, let's look at how we actually move those buyers through the journey. Kipp, I know HubSpot is the pioneer of inbound, so your standard for how buyers interact with your brand is incredibly high. You map everything to the flywheel. \n\nLinkedIn isn't just a top-of-funnel billboard. We've built an ecosystem that mirrors your exact flywheel methodology, supporting the full buyer journey from initial enterprise awareness down to closed-won pipeline. \n\nAt the awareness stage, we use Video and Sponsored Content to put your thought leadership directly in the feeds of those hard-to-reach enterprise CIOs and RevOps leaders. This builds crucial brand trust in a completely brand-safe environment. \n\nThen, as we move into consideration, we leverage Document Ads. This is perfect for the massive state-of-marketing research reports your team already produces, allowing prospects to consume high-value content right in the feed without bouncing. We pair this with Conversation Ads to drive direct, personalized engagement with your enterprise ICP.\n\nBut here is where we prove the pipeline contribution you demand. For conversion, we utilize LinkedIn Lead Gen Forms. Because these forms pre-fill with accurate, professional profile data, they completely remove the friction of manual entry. We typically see two to five times higher conversion rates with these forms compared to traditional external landing pages. \n\nIt is your inbound philosophy, accelerated by precise enterprise targeting, directly feeding your pipeline.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-8-1773281647411.wav" },
  9: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-9-1773265625301.png", narrationScript: "Looking at how this plays out in the enterprise space, let's examine a company you know incredibly well: Salesforce. Salesforce has been a highly strategic LinkedIn advertiser, specifically using our platform to drive their own enterprise platform play. They needed to reach a very specific, high-level audience that organic inbound doesn't always capture predictably at scale. For them, that meant targeting CIOs and VP-level decision-makers at massive enterprise accounts. \n\nNow, Kipp, I know you are deeply analytical and rightly skeptical of paid channels if they can't prove real pipeline contribution. You don't want cheap leads, you want revenue. That was exactly Salesforce's mindset. The key insight that drove their success here was shifting their measurement entirely away from cost-per-click, and focusing strictly on qualified pipeline. \n\nWhen they evaluated us through that lens, the numbers were definitive. By leveraging our first-party data to reach those specific enterprise VPs and CIOs, Salesforce saw a 40 percent lower cost per qualified lead compared to all their other paid channels. But more importantly for your board's upmarket growth targets, they generated a 3.2x pipeline contribution. We aren't just talking about raw leads or top-of-funnel clicks here. This is actual, high-intent pipeline that converts into closed-won enterprise revenue.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-9-1773281691195.wav" },
  10: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-10-1773265651357.png", narrationScript: "Looking at how this plays out in the real world, let's examine a company that faced the exact same upmarket challenge you're navigating right now: Drift. \n\nKipp, like HubSpot, Drift had built an incredibly strong inbound engine for the SMB space, but they needed a reliable, scalable way to break into the enterprise market. They had the thought leadership, but they needed the right delivery mechanism to reach those elusive enterprise decision-makers. \n\nTo do this, they leveraged LinkedIn Document Ads to distribute their 'Revenue Acceleration' research directly in the feed of enterprise buyers. Instead of forcing prospects to a landing page and risking drop-off, they paired this with our Lead Gen Forms. Because these forms auto-fill with accurate, real-time professional data from the member's profile, Drift seamlessly captured high-intent VP of Sales and VP of Marketing contacts without any friction. \n\nNow, as an analytical marketer, I know you're looking closely at cost-per-lead, and Drift initially had that exact same hesitation. But here is the metric that matters for your pipeline: 65% of the leads sourced from LinkedIn were accepted by their sales team. Compare that to just 30% from their other paid channels. \n\nThat massive difference in lead quality meant that even with a higher initial CPL on LinkedIn, their actual cost-per-pipeline-dollar was significantly more efficient. It proved that when you target the precise enterprise ICP with high-value content, the downstream pipeline contribution easily justifies the upfront investment.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-10-1773281744697.wav" },
  11: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-11-1773265677359.png", narrationScript: "Let's address the elephant in the room: attribution. I know proving pipeline contribution is critical for you, Kipp, and frankly, as a metrics-driven CMO scaling an enterprise motion, it absolutely should be. You've built an incredible two billion dollar inbound engine at HubSpot. If you're going to put aggressive budget behind a paid channel, you need to know it's actually driving revenue, not just capturing top-of-funnel clicks. That is exactly why LinkedIn's Conversion API is built to integrate directly with your HubSpot CRM. We aren't asking you to trust a siloed advertising dashboard. With this direct integration, you can track the complete, multi-touch buyer's journey. We're talking end-to-end visibility—from that very first enterprise ad impression, straight through to lead, MQL, opportunity, and ultimately, closed-won revenue. Our Revenue Attribution Reports will show you and your board exactly which LinkedIn campaigns generated that high-value pipeline. But the absolute best part of this setup is that the data lives right there in your HubSpot CRM. You are validating LinkedIn's performance using your own system, your own source of truth. There is no guessing game about whether our campaigns are complementing your inbound philosophy, because your own data will explicitly prove the ROI.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-11-1773281202738.wav" },
  12: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-12-1773265703701.png", narrationScript: "Now, one of the biggest hurdles in paid media is bridging the gap between top-of-funnel ad spend and bottom-of-funnel pipeline attribution. But Kipp, your own engineering team has already solved this for us. \n\nHubSpot already has a flawless, native integration with LinkedIn. In fact, your engineers built it. They built it because they recognized the unparalleled value of our professional graph. When a target enterprise prospect engages with a LinkedIn campaign, their Lead Gen Form submission syncs directly into the HubSpot CRM in real-time. It instantly creates matched contact records. It triggers your automatic workflows, and it feeds directly into your existing lead scoring models. There is no manual data export, no data decay, and no guessing if a paid lead actually converted to pipeline. \n\nThis perfectly complements your inbound philosophy. We capture their intent on LinkedIn, but the nurturing and attribution happen natively inside HubSpot where your team demands visibility. \n\nAnd because that sync is bi-directional, you can take your highly segmented HubSpot CRM data—say, a list of five hundred tier-one enterprise target accounts or a segment of stalled pipeline deals—and push it directly back into LinkedIn to build highly precise retargeting audiences. \n\nThe infrastructure is already sitting right there in your portal. We aren't talking about duct-taping two systems together to try and prove ROI to the board. We are talking about taking an engine you have already built, turning the key, and using it strategically to capture that upmarket enterprise demand.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-12-1773281244390.wav" },
  13: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-13-1773265729715.png", narrationScript: "Looking at how we operationalize this for your move upmarket, I'm not going to pitch you a massive, open-ended media buy. Rather than a broad campaign, I'm proposing a highly focused, 90-day pilot specifically targeting your hardest-to-reach enterprise ICPs. \n\nWe've structured this in three distinct phases that naturally build on each other. Kipp, think of this just like HubSpot's flywheel, but engineered specifically to accelerate paid enterprise acquisition. \n\nIn Month 1, we focus purely on awareness. We will take your absolute best inbound enterprise content and distribute it directly into the feeds of VP and C-level decision-makers. We are taking the organic value HubSpot is famous for and guaranteeing it reaches that elusive upmarket audience. \n\nThen, in Month 2, we transition into lead generation. We'll deploy LinkedIn Lead Gen Forms to capture high-intent leads from the exact accounts that engaged with your content in month one. This removes friction for the buyer and passes perfectly mapped, actionable data straight into your own CRM. \n\nBy Month 3, we execute on retargeting and conversion. We will nurture those highly engaged audiences and drive them directly toward enterprise demo requests. \n\nBecause I know pipeline attribution is your absolute baseline, we define the exact success metrics and pipeline contribution targets before we start, not after. We prove the ROI first, and only scale when the numbers justify it.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-13-1773281297030.wav" },
  14: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-14-1773265759870.png", narrationScript: "Looking at our rollout strategy, Phase 1 is designed to perfectly complement your inbound-first philosophy, Kipp. We are going to leverage the incredible content engine your team has already built. That means absolutely no new creative is needed to get this off the ground. We'll take your flagship assets, like the State of Marketing report and your high-value enterprise case studies, and amplify them using Sponsored Content. For your executive thought leadership, we'll deploy Video Ads to capture attention right in the feed. \n\nThis is exactly how we solve that upmarket board mandate. We are hyper-targeting this campaign exclusively to VP-level and above in Marketing, Sales, and RevOps, specifically at organizations with over a thousand employees. We are putting your best inbound assets directly in front of the enterprise decision-makers your organic channels might not be reaching today. \n\nBecause I know how rigorously you track performance, our Month 1 goal isn't just noise. It's establishing a highly measurable engagement baseline. We'll track reach, engagement rate, video completion rates, and crucially, direct website visits from these specific enterprise accounts. \n\nTo prove this complements your organic pipeline without over-committing, we recommend a focused Month 1 budget of approximately fifteen to twenty thousand dollars. It’s a data-driven proof of concept that shows exactly how LinkedIn can deliver the high-quality enterprise audience you need before we scale.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-14-1773281354669.wav" },
  15: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-15-1773265791835.png", narrationScript: "Building on the brand awareness we established in Phase one, Month two is where we start capturing high-intent signals and driving the enterprise pipeline you're looking for. We take the exact enterprise ICPs who engaged with your thought leadership in Month one and retarget them. This aligns perfectly with HubSpot's inbound philosophy, Kipp. We aren't cold-pitching. We are capturing demand from a warm audience that has already consumed and trusted your content. \n\nTo do this, we introduce high-value, bottom-of-funnel offers. We'll put your Enterprise ROI Calculator, the CRM Migration Guide, and Custom Demo Requests right into their feed. But here is the critical part for conversion. To ensure we don't lose these busy executives to friction, we use LinkedIn Lead Gen Forms. When that target VP of Sales or CIO clicks, their verified professional data—their name, exact job title, and company—is already pre-filled directly from their profile. It is a completely seamless experience. \n\nBecause you need to prove pipeline contribution to the board, our focus here shifts to hard, analytical metrics. We will be rigorously tracking cost per lead, the lead-to-MQL rate, and most importantly for this upmarket motion, the sales acceptance rate. To drive this qualified lead volume and prove that LinkedIn can efficiently complement your organic engine, we recommend allocating approximately twenty-five to thirty thousand dollars for Month two.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-15-1773281399155.wav" },
  16: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-16-1773265822148.png", narrationScript: "Building on the engagement we drive in Phase 2, Month 3 is where we shift focus entirely to your core metric, Kipp: pipeline conversion. This is about accelerating those engaged leads into real revenue. To do this, we’ll activate Conversation Ads for direct demo bookings. This isn't a disruptive, traditional paid play. It’s a highly personalized, conversational format that feels incredibly native to the inbound experience HubSpot pioneered, just delivered right to the LinkedIn inbox of your enterprise buyers. Simultaneously, we'll retarget the high-intent website visitors we generated earlier. But instead of generic product pitches, we’ll serve them your strongest customer testimonials and case studies, using social proof to accelerate their decision-making. To directly address that upmarket push your board is looking for, this phase leans heavily into an ABM approach. We’ll use Matched Audiences to upload your exact list of top 500 target enterprise accounts. This ensures zero ad waste. You're only paying to reach the specific buying committees at the enterprise logos that organic search alone simply can't guarantee. Because I know you need to clearly prove pipeline contribution, our KPIs here shift strictly to the bottom funnel. We'll be measuring cost per opportunity, total pipeline value generated, and demo-to-opportunity conversion rates. We recommend allocating approximately twenty to twenty-five thousand dollars for this Month 3 sprint. That budget gives us the critical mass of data to prove that LinkedIn isn't just an awareness channel, but a measurable, highly targeted extension of your enterprise revenue engine.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-16-1773281448662.wav" },
  17: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-17-1773265857980.png", narrationScript: "Let's look exactly at who we are going to reach in this pilot. I know your inbound engine is legendary, Kipp, but when we move upmarket, we need surgical precision to reach the specific buying committee that organic content doesn't always catch. \n\nHere is the exact audience specification we've built to match your enterprise ICP. For seniority, we are strictly zeroing in on VPs, Directors, and the C-suite. These are the definitive decision-makers and budget holders. We are completely filtering out the end-users to protect your ad spend and ensure high pipeline contribution. \n\nAcross functions, we're targeting Marketing, Sales, Revenue Operations, and IT. As you know better than anyone, an enterprise HubSpot deployment isn't just a marketing decision anymore—it's a massive RevOps and IT commitment. We need to surround that entire buying committee simultaneously. \n\nFor company size, we are looking exclusively at the 1,000 to 10,000, and 10,000-plus employee tiers. This is true enterprise territory. We're applying this across North America, the UK, and the DACH region, specifically within Technology, Financial Services, Healthcare, and Manufacturing. These are the exact verticals where we see the highest velocity for enterprise CRM adoption on LinkedIn right now. \n\nBy layering these precise filters, we guarantee that every dollar of this pilot is spent solely on high-intent enterprise buyers, directly answering your concern about audience quality versus cost. \n\nKipp, looking at this exact matrix of titles, sizes, and industries—does this match the ICP your enterprise sales team is actively pursuing right now?", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-17-1773281506007.wav" },
  18: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-18-1773265884552.png", narrationScript: "Now, let's look at exactly what it takes to execute this strategy and prove that pipeline contribution. We are proposing a 90-day pilot with a total investment of $60,000 to $75,000. I want to be clear, Kipp: we are not asking for a massive, year-long commitment right out of the gate. This is a highly controlled, 90-day test designed with strict go/no-go criteria tied directly to the pipeline metrics you care about most. \n\nWe've structured this spend across three distinct phases to seamlessly complement your inbound methodology. Phase one is Awareness, where we'll allocate 15 to 20K to build that highly targeted enterprise audience foundation, reaching the exact buying committees organic search might miss. Phase two is Lead Generation. This is our primary conversion phase and the largest slice of the investment at 25 to 30K, focusing strictly on capturing high-intent enterprise demand. Finally, Phase three is Conversion and pipeline acceleration, utilizing the remaining 20 to 25K to nurture those mid-to-bottom funnel accounts until they are fully sales-ready.\n\nYou and I both know that HubSpot's enterprise ACV sits well over the $100K mark. When we frame this pilot against your typical customer lifetime value, the math becomes incredibly compelling. Just one closed-won enterprise deal sourced from this pilot pays for the entire 90-day investment multiple times over. It is a low-risk, high-upside framework to definitively prove that LinkedIn can drive the upmarket, enterprise growth the board is pushing for, without compromising your inbound-first philosophy.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-18-1773281568538.wav" },
  19: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-19-1773265914998.png", narrationScript: "Let's talk about the most critical part of this entire proposal: how we actually measure success. Kipp, I know your team is incredibly metrics-driven. Coming from an inbound-first philosophy, you rightly demand that any paid channel proves its undeniable contribution to pipeline. That's why we need to agree on exactly how we'll measure success before we start spending a single dollar, not after. \n\nFor our primary metrics, we are looking strictly at bottom-funnel impact. We will track pipeline created directly from LinkedIn-sourced leads, your cost per qualified opportunity, and the sales acceptance rate. We have to prove that the enterprise ICPs we're targeting are turning into real, workable pipeline for your sales team. \n\nAs leading indicators, our secondary metrics will monitor our reach into your specific target accounts, the overall engagement rate, and the quality of website visits coming from those enterprise buyers. We need to ensure we are engaging the exact upmarket accounts that your organic channels might not be capturing today. \n\nThe best part is that every piece of this data flows natively into your own HubSpot CRM. There is no black box here. You own the measurement entirely, and we'll be looking at your dashboards, not ours. \n\nWe've also built in a hard checkpoint at Day 60. We will sit down, review the data from Phases 1 and 2, and make a clear go or no-go decision on moving into Phase 3. If the pipeline isn't there, we don't scale. \n\nLooking at this framework, Kipp, are there any other specific metrics your team would want to track?", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-19-1773281627378.wav" },
  20: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-20-1773265943685.png", narrationScript: "Building on our pipeline discussion, Kipp, I want to address something I know matters deeply to you and the entire HubSpot marketing team: brand safety. You've spent nearly two decades building HubSpot into a two-billion-dollar inbound powerhouse rooted in trust. When you push aggressively into paid channels to capture that enterprise upmarket motion, you simply cannot risk placing that hard-earned brand equity next to the wrong content. \n\nThat is exactly why LinkedIn is the only major ad platform where the feed is exclusively professional. Unlike other networks where you're constantly fighting algorithms to avoid the latest viral outrage, we ensure your ads have zero exposure to misinformation, toxic political debates, or controversial adjacent placements. \n\nInstead, when a VP of Sales or a RevOps leader sees your enterprise campaign, it appears directly alongside high-value industry insights, career development content, and strategic business discussions. It actually reinforces your inbound philosophy of educating and providing value to the market. \n\nAnd because you are highly analytical and demand rigorous standards, our brand suitability controls let you choose exactly where your content appears. You hold the reins. You have built a premium enterprise platform, Kipp. This is the premium, trusted brand environment that HubSpot's reputation absolutely deserves.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-20-1773281683914.wav" },
  21: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-21-1773265972074.png", narrationScript: "Looking at the implementation timeline, I know one of your biggest concerns with launching a new enterprise paid motion is the operational drag it might put on your team. We've designed this process so we can go from sign-off to live campaigns in exactly two weeks, with virtually no heavy lifting from your side. We handle the execution, the setup, and the ongoing optimization.\n\nIn Week 1, my team takes the wheel. We finalize the account setup and configure those highly specific enterprise audience segments we just discussed. Since HubSpot already has a world-class inbound engine, we aren't asking you to create net-new assets. We simply select the highest-converting pieces from your existing content library to fuel this motion.\n\nMoving into Week 2, we conduct a final creative review. More importantly, this is when we lock in the attribution. We set up the conversion tracking and rigorously verify the HubSpot CRM integration. Kipp, I know proving pipeline contribution is non-negotiable for you and the board, so we do not launch until we confirm campaign data is flowing perfectly back into your own dashboards. \n\nBy Week 3, we hit the launch button on our Phase 1 awareness content. Throughout this entire pilot, you will have a dedicated LinkedIn account team acting as a direct extension of your marketing org. We do the heavy lifting of account setup and optimization, ensuring your team stays focused on what they do best—driving that core inbound growth—while we systematically capture that upmarket enterprise demand.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-21-1773281736188.wav" },
  22: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-22-1773265998076.png", narrationScript: "Now, looking at how we actually execute this enterprise motion, I want to be very clear about what happens the moment we launch. This pilot comes with full white-glove support. Kipp, you're not just getting a login to a self-serve ad account and being left to figure it out. We treat this as a true strategic partnership. \n\nYou will have a dedicated account manager serving as your single point of contact, ensuring every dollar spent aligns with your strict pipeline requirements. Alongside them is your dedicated campaign strategist. Because your team is highly analytical and needs to prove ROI, this strategist is constantly in the weeds, providing proactive targeting and optimization recommendations so we are capturing the exact upmarket ICPs that your organic engine might miss. \n\nWe also know HubSpot creates world-class inbound content. To maximize that existing investment, we include ongoing creative consultations. Our team will work directly with yours to optimize ad formats and adapt your messaging specifically for the LinkedIn feed, maintaining complete brand safety. \n\nAnd to keep us absolutely accountable to your board's growth targets, we anchor this partnership with rigorous Quarterly Business Reviews. We'll sit down, look at the hard attribution data, and align our strategy directly to your revenue performance. Ultimately, you're getting direct, unfiltered access to LinkedIn's deepest B2B marketing expertise, ensuring this paid motion flawlessly complements your inbound-first philosophy.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-22-1773282140232.wav" },
  23: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-23-1773266026155.png", narrationScript: "Looking at the timeline, Kipp, you might be asking why we need to pull the trigger on this pilot right now. There are three strategic reasons why this exact moment is the inflection point for HubSpot. \n\nFirst, your upmarket motion is accelerating. With the Clearbit acquisition, the expansion of Operations Hub, and your aggressive hiring of enterprise sales reps, you have built the infrastructure to close much larger deals. But organic inbound alone won't feed those enterprise reps fast enough. You need targeted, account-based demand to support that specific motion. \n\nSecond, the market isn't waiting. Your competitors are already heavily investing in LinkedIn for enterprise reach. They are actively targeting the exact CIOs and RevOps leaders you need, using our platform to bypass the organic noise and get right in front of the buying committee. \n\nThird, and most critically for an analytical team like yours, is the calendar. By launching this pilot now, we generate 90 days of hard, pipeline-attributed data right before you lock in annual budget planning. You won't be guessing about Q1 allocations. If this pilot works and proves the pipeline contribution we've modeled, you will have the empirical proof you need to scale confidently. If it doesn't? You've invested a fraction of the ACV of one single enterprise deal to learn that. The upside is a predictable enterprise growth engine, while the downside is a highly controlled, inexpensive learning exercise.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-23-1773282653892.wav" },
  24: { imageUrl: "/uploads/pitch-slides/pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-24-1773266054518.png", narrationScript: "Kipp, I appreciate the time you've taken today to discuss how LinkedIn can support HubSpot's growth. As we look to the future, I want to outline some clear next steps that will set us up for success together.\n\nThis week, let’s align on your ideal customer profile and the key success metrics that matter most to your team. I’ll send over a concise one-page brief to make this process seamless. \n\nThen, in the following week, we can dive into account setup and select content from your existing library that resonates with our targeted audience. This is where we’ll ensure that the messaging reflects HubSpot’s core values while tapping into LinkedIn’s unique capabilities. \n\nBy week three, we’ll be ready to launch Phase 1 of our awareness campaigns. This is where we’ll start to see the impact of our efforts. I suggest we schedule a performance check-in at Day 30 to assess how everything is tracking and make adjustments if necessary. \n\nFinally, at Day 60, we’ll conduct a formal go/no-go review before we advance to Phase 3. This structured approach ensures we’re closely monitoring pipeline contributions and aligning with your inbound-first philosophy.\n\nCan we schedule a follow-up this week to finalize the ICP and success metrics? I’m excited about the potential for HubSpot and LinkedIn to work together and make a meaningful impact.", narrationAudioUrl: "/uploads/narration/narration-pitch-hubspot-linkedin-pilot-24-1773267923547.wav" },
};

